Ladybird checks an iframe’s navigation against the frame-src of the
iframe’s container document, whichever document started it, and reports
a violation in that document. The initiating document’s policy still
governs form-action and upgrade-insecure-requests for the navigation.

All three engines do the same. Blink’s NavigationRequest::
CheckCSPDirectives checks frame-src against the parent frame’s policies
(parent_policies), and uses the initiator’s only for form-action. The
isAllowedByContentSecurityPolicy() function in WebKit’s PolicyChecker
checks the policy of the owner element’s document, through its
allowChildFrameFromSource. And Gecko’s CSPService::ConsultCSP() uses
LoadInfo::GetPolicyContainer(), whose policy container for a frame load
is that of the frame element’s owner document.
